##### BlowUp #####

$$TableOfContents$$

#### Introduction ####

BlowUp is a low friction markup language with an almost WYSIWYG plain-text formatting syntax for the most common situations writers encounter, and a set of extensions with a coherent JSON-based data model for the less common ones. Inspiration for its design has been taken from [[AsciiDoc::https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AsciiDoc]], [[DocBook::https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DocBook]], [[LaTeX::https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LaTeX]], [[Markdown::https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Markdown]], [[MathML::https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MathML]], [[Plain Old Documentation::https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plain_Old_Documentation]], [[reStructuredText::https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ReStructuredText]], [[Scalable Vector Graphics::https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scalable_Vector_Graphics]], [[Scribe::https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scribe_(markup_language)]], [[TeX::https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TeX]], [[Texinfo::https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Texinfo]] and [[Troff::https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Troff]].

This document is both a specification of the BlowUp language and a functional test for its parser.

#### A Level 2 Title ####

There are five available hierarchy levels.

