Here is how some formulas can be written:

H₂O A₀₁₂₃₄₅₆₇₈₉B 10⁻⁴ A⁺⁻⁽⁰¹²³⁴⁵⁶⁷⁸⁹⁾ⁿB αβγδεηθλμπρ ≡≈±×÷⁄≤≥≠

Here is how quote blocks can be written:

> Aenean convallis mauris tellus, eget feugiat erat lobortis sed. Mauris risus augue, pellentesque nec semper porta, sodales ac nisi. Suspendisse eu elit nulla. Morbi sagittis dolor sit amet nisl porta, suscipit viverra urna interdum. Nulla faucibus felis vitae tellus lobortis, ac mattis elit congue. Mauris hendrerit ex vel justo fermentum, et hendrerit velit aliquet. Suspendisse potenti. Orci varius natoque penatibus et magnis dis parturient montes, nascetur ridiculus mus. Quisque maximus auctor mi, sed semper nunc ullamcorper sit amet.
>
> (Marcus Tullius Cicero)

Here is how ordered lists can be written:

    1. Element A
    2. Element B
    3. Element C

Here is how unordered lists can be written:

    * Element A
    * Element B
    * Element C

In ordered and unordered lists indentation matters and must consist of blocks of exactly 4 spaces:

    * Element A
        * Element A.1
            1. Element A.1.1
            2. Element A.1.2
        * Element A.2
        * Element A.3
    * Element B
        * Element B.1
        * Element B.2
    * Element C
        1. Element C.1
        2. Element C.2
        3. Element C.3

Here is how links can be written:

    * [[Google::https://www.google.com]]
    * [[Microsoft::https://www.microsoft.com]]

Or:

    * [[https://www.google.com]]
    * [[https://www.microsoft.com]]

Or: (all the links below should appear on the same line)

[[Google::https://www.google.com]], [[https://www.google.com]], [[Microsoft::https://www.microsoft.com]], [[https://www.microsoft.com]], [[BlowUp]].

Here is how images, which are responsive by default, can be included:

||This is a test image.::TestImage1.jpg||

Here is how data tables can be written (text alignment in columns is determined by the use of spaces):

| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| Pos | City                                                 | Country   |  Population |
| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
|  1  | [[Beijing::https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beijing]]   | China PR  |  21,542,000 |
|  2  | [[Tokyo::https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tokyo]]       | Japan     |  13,929,000 |
|  3  | [[Moscow::https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moscow]]     | Russia    |  12,506,000 |
|  4  | [[Kinshasa::https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kinshasa]] | DR Congo  |  11,855,000 |
|  5  | [[Jakarta::https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jakarta]]   | Indonesia |  10,075,000 |
| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |

Or:

┌─────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┬───────────┬─────────────┐
│ Pos │ City                                                 │ Country   │  Population │
├─────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────┼─────────────┤
│  1  │ [[Beijing::https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beijing]]   │ China PR  │  21,542,000 │
│  2  │ [[Tokyo::https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tokyo]]       │ Japan     │  13,929,000 │
│  3  │ [[Moscow::https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moscow]]     │ Russia    │  12,506,000 │
│  4  │ [[Kinshasa::https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kinshasa]] │ DR Congo  │  11,855,000 │
│  5  │ [[Jakarta::https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jakarta]]   │ Indonesia │  10,075,000 │
└─────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┴───────────┴─────────────┘

Here is how code blocks can be written:

` Hello!
` This is a code block.
`     Indentation is of course preserved.
`     Inside a code block all transformations should be **disabled (you should not see this as bold)**.
`     It must be possible to enter literals like [[http://www.google.com]] and <script>alert('You should not see this as an alert!');</script>.
` Bye.

Backticks can be used for inline code like ``System.IO.File`` or for literals like ``[[http://www.google.com]]`` (you should not see this as a link) and ``<script>alert('You should not see this as an alert!');</script>``.

